secubox-soc (1.0.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Capture production SOC dashboard back into source. Prior to this
    bump, packages/secubox-soc/www/soc/index.html in the source tree
    (44 KB, "threat-map" design, talks to /api/v1/soc/*) did NOT match
    what was actually running on production boards (107 KB
    "comprehensive dashboard" that aggregates /api/v1/hub,
    /api/v1/waf, /api/v1/crowdsec, /api/v1/hub/public/firewall_summary).
    The board version was being maintained out-of-tree and dpkg
    couldn't redeploy it. This bump pulls the 107 KB dashboard back
    into source as the canonical SOC frontend.

  * While re-syncing: strip the dead `.logo`, `.logo-icon`,
    `.logo-text`, `.logo-version` CSS overrides at the top of the
    file. The .logo-icon rule in particular re-styled the lock emoji
    that sidebar.js injects into the sidebar header as a 40x40
    gradient-box, breaking visual consistency with every other module.
    The shared /shared/sidebar.css owns those classes — let it.

 -- Gerald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Tue, 26 May 2026 13:00:00 +0000

